diff --git a/packages/client/modules/tests/ADDITIVE-LIVE.md b/packages/client/modules/tests/ADDITIVE-LIVE.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..4d86df60
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/client/modules/tests/ADDITIVE-LIVE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# ISSUE-028 bounded production additive graph
+
+This candidate adds ordinary Web metadata subscription, not development code HMR. The Host publishes its current graph immediately on same-origin SSE connection and after graph changes. The client validates the whole snapshot before adding any module rows, then uses existing prefetch and native Loader creation. Existing module/plugin metadata changes, removal and reordering reject the snapshot with needs-restart; later valid snapshots remain admissible. No page reload is performed.
+
+The wire only admits canonical package IDs and `/plugins/<id>/client.js?rev=<12-hex>` URLs. `/client` remains the existing module-system alias, so a root package whose name collides with that suffix is not newly supported. Static seed and bootstrap identities cannot be replaced. Current authority is privately copied. A factory that throws receives a tombstone until explicit invalidate (the separate development contract); another module cannot replay it through require.
+
+The consumer keeps one latest pending snapshot and one execution queue. Transport prefetch failures can retry on later snapshots; after Loader creation starts, failures are not implicitly replayed. Each prefetch/create wait is bounded to 30 seconds and cancelled at scope disposal. The Loader owner tracks only its newly created IDs, drains normal cleanup and preserves initial entries. Non-cooperative arbitrary JavaScript cannot be forcibly terminated in-process: cleanup exceeding 5 seconds reports needs-restart and must not be called a successful unload.
+
+Standalone Linux Node24 regression: `TSX_TSCONFIG_PATH=$PWD/tsconfig.live-smoke.json node --import tsx/esm --test packages/client/modules/tests/additive-live.smoke.ts`. Nine tests cover hostile/changed snapshots, recovery, real Loader identity/disposal, pending prefetch/create cancellation, cooperative late apply, failed factory dependency replay and real HTTP SSE reconnect/disposal. These are not the complete upstream coverage/browser gates.
+
+Small strict emit: `tsc -p tsconfig.live-modules.json`; then from this package use its original `tsdown.config.ts` to build both faces. Only installed rc2 dependencies and existing build tools are linked; no full monorepo installation or compilation is needed. Browser acceptance must separately verify an existing tab gains the real AutoReview entry without refresh and can persist settings. At this commit that second browser acceptance is still pending; earlier Eawiaf proved backend activation but failed same-tab arrival before this candidate.
